# Existing planner state safety

The current planner uses a TypeScript GraphEnvelope and explicit node execution in [graph.ts](base/planner-ts/src/graph.ts). It is not the removed Python StateGraph implementation. Read the actual node contract before changing state propagation.

- Preserve required state on success, early return, error and timeout paths. Do not assume a library automatically merges fields.
- Use the current [state types](base/planner-ts/src/state/types.ts) and [reducer helpers](base/planner-ts/src/state/reducers.ts); do not recreate Python state.py or graph.py wrappers.
- Check both the field a node writes and the transition that consumes it. Cover relevant alternate routes with behavioral tests.
- A timeout response does not itself cancel underlying work. Propagate cancellation to external calls where supported and prevent late work from publishing state after termination.
- Keep source provenance and caller scope attached to evidence. State merging is not authorization.

These rules apply to maintenance of this graph, not to the architecture of new knowledge tools. The [architecture decision record](docs/ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md) does not retain a mandatory planning graph.
